[[:db/retract 17592186118280 :answer-field/choices 17592186118281] [:db/retract 17592186118280 :answer-field/choices 17592186118282] [:db/retract 17592186118280 :answer-field/choices 17592186118283] [:db/retract 17592186118280 :answer-field/choices 17592186118284] [:db/retract 17592186118280 :answer-field/choices 17592186118285] {:db/id 17592186119823 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5f9af9de-03ce-5718-9ed4-8f070e270c5e" "question-2f3e71ae-af49-5472-af32-b57e5521039a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119824 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0b15402b-e686-556b-80b9-873d877b7aa1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1f3bd7e4-e9ee-5ec1-b495-697d442c712e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119636 :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $\\mathbf{b}$'s in terms of $\\mathbf{c}$'s. Multiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{c}_1+\\mathbf{c}_2 = -\\mathbf{b}_2\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{b}_2 = -2\\mathbf{c}_1-\\mathbf{c}_2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c}_1 = \\left( -2\\mathbf{c}_1-\\mathbf{c}_2 \\right) - \\mathbf{b}_1\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{b}_1 = -3\\mathbf{c}_1-\\mathbf{c}_2.\n$$\n\nSince ![](images/0e/0e283c9948eacf3e231eef3a3feb355c33f20c3dbfd89e97c530331758af34ad.svg) we can write the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf c_1$ and $\\mathbf c_2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =(-3{c}_{1}-{c}_{2})-3(-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =-3{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+6{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2} \\\\  & =3{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/d8/d8d25ca46df4435c67e7c23e61851e2acd4826b0b2d99d9b54de8b6f2c37ee94.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f9af9de-03ce-5718-9ed4-8f070e270c5e" :question/id #uuid "5f9af9de-03ce-5718-9ed4-8f070e270c5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35261" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-8{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}+6{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-(-4{b}_{2})+2(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-8{b}_{2})+2(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-83cc079b-0440-5af9-a279-b83e4c99c769"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-83cc079b-0440-5af9-a279-b83e4c99c769" :answer-field/id #uuid "83cc079b-0440-5af9-a279-b83e4c99c769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-805154d8-bb48-5c28-8787-0a43308ed66d" "answer-591225ac-bd90-5ecb-bd8a-ea3b808b5e20" "answer-50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" "answer-c63964c0-5683-5c24-a2a1-075e70846087" "answer-92932d78-c613-5c42-8f32-7950ba738ba0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-805154d8-bb48-5c28-8787-0a43308ed66d" :answer/id #uuid "805154d8-bb48-5c28-8787-0a43308ed66d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-591225ac-bd90-5ecb-bd8a-ea3b808b5e20" :answer/id #uuid "591225ac-bd90-5ecb-bd8a-ea3b808b5e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" :answer/id #uuid "50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c63964c0-5683-5c24-a2a1-075e70846087" :answer/id #uuid "c63964c0-5683-5c24-a2a1-075e70846087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92932d78-c613-5c42-8f32-7950ba738ba0" :answer/id #uuid "92932d78-c613-5c42-8f32-7950ba738ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247301 :question/problem "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f3e71ae-af49-5472-af32-b57e5521039a" :question/id #uuid "2f3e71ae-af49-5472-af32-b57e5521039a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34773" :question/problem "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=4{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-2{c}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-5({c}_{2})+3(-{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(4{c}_{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(-2{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}{b}_{1}+\\frac{3}{2}{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d65567a-61e9-526a-b757-4f395c20b9a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d65567a-61e9-526a-b757-4f395c20b9a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d65567a-61e9-526a-b757-4f395c20b9a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-198e300a-44d0-5694-88ed-2170ad2ca1e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4b29cca-110e-5949-a6ce-e19ab93bd9d6" "answer-404cd653-49d5-53d4-97a1-86fa615b47b5" "answer-559920af-21be-5fab-b579-0d1866bc1809" "answer-198e300a-44d0-5694-88ed-2170ad2ca1e0" "answer-dd47cc6e-7faa-5406-9624-2956e3795db8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4b29cca-110e-5949-a6ce-e19ab93bd9d6" :answer/id #uuid "f4b29cca-110e-5949-a6ce-e19ab93bd9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-404cd653-49d5-53d4-97a1-86fa615b47b5" :answer/id #uuid "404cd653-49d5-53d4-97a1-86fa615b47b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-559920af-21be-5fab-b579-0d1866bc1809" :answer/id #uuid "559920af-21be-5fab-b579-0d1866bc1809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-198e300a-44d0-5694-88ed-2170ad2ca1e0" :answer/id #uuid "198e300a-44d0-5694-88ed-2170ad2ca1e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd47cc6e-7faa-5406-9624-2956e3795db8" :answer/id #uuid "dd47cc6e-7faa-5406-9624-2956e3795db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120383 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=4{b}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351266 :question/problem "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=2{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-5{c}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186382427 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=2{b}_{2}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351269 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-6{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b15402b-e686-556b-80b9-873d877b7aa1" :question/id #uuid "0b15402b-e686-556b-80b9-873d877b7aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80822" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-7{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{3}=-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={b}_{1}+10{b}_{2}-7{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{3}+10{b}_{2}+{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{3}+5(2{b}_{2})-(-{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7ba0e4d8-f543-552a-b200-356460576b1a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7ba0e4d8-f543-552a-b200-356460576b1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba0e4d8-f543-552a-b200-356460576b1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fa973209-e94d-50bd-9a41-51a05e29d130" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f7f09aa-2e3d-594f-a78e-cfa9079c7c21" "answer-5344465e-848e-5743-88e1-874c6d5aa3ef" "answer-ed2e3705-b2d7-5c5d-a3f1-92769931cf3c" "answer-fa973209-e94d-50bd-9a41-51a05e29d130" "answer-4407bb99-7be8-580d-91b8-439544a0058a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f7f09aa-2e3d-594f-a78e-cfa9079c7c21" :answer/id #uuid "1f7f09aa-2e3d-594f-a78e-cfa9079c7c21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5344465e-848e-5743-88e1-874c6d5aa3ef" :answer/id #uuid "5344465e-848e-5743-88e1-874c6d5aa3ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed2e3705-b2d7-5c5d-a3f1-92769931cf3c" :answer/id #uuid "ed2e3705-b2d7-5c5d-a3f1-92769931cf3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa973209-e94d-50bd-9a41-51a05e29d130" :answer/id #uuid "fa973209-e94d-50bd-9a41-51a05e29d130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4407bb99-7be8-580d-91b8-439544a0058a" :answer/id #uuid "4407bb99-7be8-580d-91b8-439544a0058a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410058 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}={b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-2({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120361 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=(-{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-3(-{c}_{2})+4({c}_{1}+{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{c}_{2}+4{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}+7{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118280 :answer-field/correct "answer-4c342d58-92e7-533b-8f8a-f85d38cc91c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ac17bbb1-ef71-5066-9361-5ab9de0c1d4d" "answer-4c342d58-92e7-533b-8f8a-f85d38cc91c4" "answer-ab88d19a-3124-5017-a14e-eded936a6b24" "answer-4b460d7d-05fc-5b15-8765-b5b270de1457" "answer-b8489fb5-7510-5290-99ff-82eff74dc7d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac17bbb1-ef71-5066-9361-5ab9de0c1d4d" :answer/id #uuid "ac17bbb1-ef71-5066-9361-5ab9de0c1d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c342d58-92e7-533b-8f8a-f85d38cc91c4" :answer/id #uuid "4c342d58-92e7-533b-8f8a-f85d38cc91c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab88d19a-3124-5017-a14e-eded936a6b24" :answer/id #uuid "ab88d19a-3124-5017-a14e-eded936a6b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b460d7d-05fc-5b15-8765-b5b270de1457" :answer/id #uuid "4b460d7d-05fc-5b15-8765-b5b270de1457" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8489fb5-7510-5290-99ff-82eff74dc7d8" :answer/id #uuid "b8489fb5-7510-5290-99ff-82eff74dc7d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351165 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+6(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-5{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-5({c}_{2}-2{c}_{1})+2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-5{c}_{2}+10{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{3} \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-1f3bd7e4-e9ee-5ec1-b495-697d442c712e" :question/id #uuid "1f3bd7e4-e9ee-5ec1-b495-697d442c712e" :question/math-academy-id "q-113070" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2(-{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-(-{c}_{2})+3({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & ={c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4c066721-df4d-58dc-9748-1ef1119a9c18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c066721-df4d-58dc-9748-1ef1119a9c18" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c066721-df4d-58dc-9748-1ef1119a9c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6599960a-b761-54ae-800a-4099e8dc6454" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7960b759-a049-517f-91ce-8f3d3d4ab81c" "answer-06929580-b4ba-53af-ac69-8bc84360d71e" "answer-6599960a-b761-54ae-800a-4099e8dc6454" "answer-7238f33a-029e-5920-a373-cb968bcc10aa" "answer-8d5905dd-9d56-563e-ab3a-014628903d88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7960b759-a049-517f-91ce-8f3d3d4ab81c" :answer/id #uuid "7960b759-a049-517f-91ce-8f3d3d4ab81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06929580-b4ba-53af-ac69-8bc84360d71e" :answer/id #uuid "06929580-b4ba-53af-ac69-8bc84360d71e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6599960a-b761-54ae-800a-4099e8dc6454" :answer/id #uuid "6599960a-b761-54ae-800a-4099e8dc6454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7238f33a-029e-5920-a373-cb968bcc10aa" :answer/id #uuid "7238f33a-029e-5920-a373-cb968bcc10aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d5905dd-9d56-563e-ab3a-014628903d88" :answer/id #uuid "8d5905dd-9d56-563e-ab3a-014628903d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
